00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:12.049 align:start position:0%
overwatch is competitive mode has  finally arrived on the public test realm  and with it it brings an entirely new  system of ranked play to the game the  way the matches work in this mode is  each team takes turns attacking and the  score is based upon how many points they  actually capture after each team has a  chance to attack the scores are tallied  and the team with the most wins how it  differs from quick play is that if the  score is tied they go into sudden death  in that the attacking team is decided by  a coin flip and will have two minutes to  capture a single point after you play  the ten placement matches the game will  assign you a skill rating and will use  that number to find a group with a  similar average it's this method of  matchmaking that makes a mode feel  competitive you will end up playing with  people who are actually on the same  level as you skill wise instead of  whatever number is below the portrait  the mode self feels frantic exhilarating  knowing that the matches mean something  but it also does a lot to put the focus  of the game on the actual objectives  during payload for example the  individual checkpoints are a lot more  valuable this time around now that  capturing and defending those points  determines an actual score players will  want to keep a closer watch and protect  them at all costs and by putting  people's ranks at stake as they can rise  and fall from match to match the mode  seems to encourage people to care about  the game and not go running off to try  to keep their kill streak going it's all  about teamwork here and even playing on  the public test realm I could sense  people were trying really hard to work  together and to help the team succeed  the group matchmaking seems like it will  work particularly well and will give the  players the balance and even matches  they've been waiting for since the game  was released and with new rewards during  each three-month long season of  competitive mode including exclusive  icons sprays and holy crab gold weapons  it's bound to have people come flocking  back to the game the new mode is still  in its testing phase as Blizzard is  continuing to work out some balance  issues with the sudden death portion of  the game but it'll hopefully be released  within the next month so in the meantime  boot up overwatch hop on the PTR and  test the mode out for yourself
 

